      "headline": {
        "en": "Chicago Leads CMBS Distress Among 11 MLB Playoff Metros",
        "zh": "芝加哥在11个MLB季后赛都会区中CMBS困境居首"
      },
      "summary": {
        "en": "As of August, 25.3 percent of the Chicago metro's outstanding CMBS balance was delinquent or in special servicing, the highest of the 11 Major League Baseball playoff metro areas and up 4.7 percentage points in a year, according to CRED iQ. The $536 million loan on Chicago's Aon Center reached maturity in July and wasn't repaid, and a three-year extension request was denied. Nationally, the CMBS distress rate was 10.9 percent in August, down from 11.5 percent a year earlier, preliminary September numbers point to 10.8 percent, and office accounts for 45.5 percent of distressed balance.",
        "zh": "据CRED iQ，截至8月，芝加哥都会区未偿CMBS余额中有25.3%处于逾期或特殊服务状态，在11个美国职业棒球大联盟季后赛都会区中最高，同比上升4.7个百分点。芝加哥Aon Center的5.36亿美元贷款于7月到期未偿还，三年期展期请求被拒。全国范围，8月CMBS困境率为10.9%，低于上年同期的11.5%，9月初值为10.8%，其中写字楼占困境余额的45.5%。"
      },
